# Wave 6, editor-annotations. The composition site -- where the tool, the
# gesture, the editor and the command context are actually wired together.
#
# This is the file that makes the rest of the pillar real. Everything else
# here is a pure function or a component; without this decl they exist and
# nothing reaches them.

file: "packages/editor/src/canvas/canvas.tsx"
doc: "The canvas: one SVG, three layers, and the owner of pointer and keyboard routing."

constants: [
  { name: "Canvas"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Five additions.\n"
      "\n"
      "ANCHOR GRIP HIT. The pointerdown path already computes `onHandle` via\n"
      "handleAtPoint; it now also computes `onAnchorGrip` via anchorGripAt and\n"
      "puts it in the PressContext. Both radii are screen pixels divided by\n"
      "zoom, as handleAtPoint already requires.\n"
      "\n"
      "TWO NEW DECISIONS. 'create-annotation' applies addAnnotationEdit at the\n"
      "press point in DIAGRAM coordinates, with newAnnotationId and\n"
      "NEW_ANNOTATION_TEXT, then selects it and opens its text editor.\n"
      "'anchor' starts an AnchorSession and is wired exactly as move and\n"
      "resize are: anchorUpdate on each pointermove, feeding the overlay's\n"
      "`anchorLine` prop, and anchorCommit on pointerup. The hit passed to\n"
      "both is hitTestPoint at the current pointer. No decision logic lives\n"
      "here; this decl only wires.\n"
      "\n"
      "DOUBLE-CLICK, detected from `pointerdown` via `event.detail === 2`,\n"
      "NOT from a dblclick listener. The first line of onPointerDown is\n"
      "event.preventDefault(), which suppresses the compatibility mouse\n"
      "events -- click and dblclick among them -- so a dblclick handler here\n"
      "would never fire.\n"
      "\n"
      "The condition is `event.detail === 2` AND the hit is an annotation.\n"
      "That press opens the text editor and starts no move gesture. A press\n"
      "with detail 1 on an already-selected annotation is an ordinary press\n"
      "and still starts a move -- dragging a selected annotation must keep\n"
      "working.\n"
      "\n"
      "DIMMING. The diagram layer currently dims only during a move, and only\n"
      "the moved refs. Extend it to also dim any annotation whose callout the\n"
      "overlay is previewing -- otherwise dragging a callout TARGET, or\n"
      "resizing either end, leaves the painted callout at full opacity while\n"
      "the overlay paints a second one over it. calloutPreviews reports which\n"
      "annotations those are, by id.\n"
      "\n"
      "TEXT EDITOR. Render TextEditor when ui.textEditTarget() is set,\n"
      "positioned from the scene bounds of that ref, inside the pan/zoom group\n"
      "so it tracks the canvas.\n"
      "\n"
      "The scene is an async resource, so for at least one rebuild after an\n"
      "annotation is created its ref is NOT in geometry.byKey. Do not wait for\n"
      "it -- gating the editor on bounds existing drops the autofocus that\n"
      "makes create-then-type work at all. Open the editor immediately at the\n"
      "bounds the creating gesture already knows: a Bounds whose top-left is\n"
      "the position passed to addAnnotationEdit and whose extent is\n"
      "NEW_ANNOTATION_SIZE. Once the ref appears in geometry.byKey, use those\n"
      "bounds instead -- the editor moves to the real box on the next scene,\n"
      "which is one frame and not worth avoiding. Commit applies setAnnotationTextEdit and\n"
      "clears the target; cancel clears the target only. An annotation that\n"
      "was just created and is cancelled without typing is left in place with\n"
      "its placeholder text -- undo removes it, and silently deleting on\n"
      "cancel would make Escape mean two different things.\n"
      "\n"
      "COMMAND CONTEXT. The one built here gains `beginTextEdit`: if the ref's\n"
      "scene bounds are not entirely inside the container rect, pan the\n"
      "viewport so the ref's centre is at the container's centre; then set\n"
      "ui.setTextEditTarget. When the bounds are already fully visible, or the\n"
      "ref is not in the scene index yet, pan nothing and just set the target.\n"
      "\n"
      "This is the editor's only production construction site for that\n"
      "context, so a field left unset here is a command that silently does\n"
      "nothing."
    type: { unsupported: { reason: RAW_EXPRESSION, source_excerpt: "Component<CanvasProps>" } }
    uses: ["CanvasProps", "routePress", "anchorGripAt", "handleAtPoint", "hitTestPoint", "TextEditor", "addAnnotationEdit", "setAnnotationTextEdit", "newAnnotationId", "NEW_ANNOTATION_TEXT", "NEW_ANNOTATION_SIZE", "anchorUpdate", "anchorCommit", "AnchorSession", "calloutPreviews", "OverlayLayer", "DiagramLayer", "elementKey"]
  }
]
